## Keyboard Controls

- `W` — Move forward
- `S` — Move backward
- `A` — Turn left
- `D` — Turn right
- `Q` — Quit

## Explanation

- `rospy.init_node()` initializes the ROS node.
- `Publisher()` publishes velocity commands to `/turtle1/cmd_vel`.
- `Twist` contains linear and angular velocity values.
- `termios` and `tty` allow the program to read keyboard input directly.
- `linear.x` controls forward and backward movement.
- `angular.z` controls rotation.
- `pub.publish(Twist())` sends zero velocity to stop the turtle.
- `rospy.is_shutdown()` checks whether ROS is shutting down.
- `finally` restores the terminal settings when the program exits.

## Expected Result

The turtle moves forward, backward, and turns based on keyboard input. Pressing `Q` exits the program.
